
# 3. Stack Using Array

## Question Description
Implement a stack using an array in C++. Perform push and pop operations and display the stack elements. A stack follows the Last In, First Out (LIFO) principle.

## Test Cases

### Test Case 1
Operations: `Push(10), Push(20), Push(30), Pop()`

Expected Output:
`Popped element: 30`

### Test Case 2
Operations: `Push(5), Push(15), Pop()`

Expected Output:
`Popped element: 15`

### Test Case 3
Operations: `Push(7), Pop()`

Expected Output:
`Popped element: 7`

## Time Complexity
- Push: O(1)
- Pop: O(1)
- Display: O(n)

## Space Complexity
- O(n), where n is the stack capacity.
